  "question": {
    "text": "A plano-convex lens <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> has a radius of curvature <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;and is placed at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> from a concave lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> as shown. At what distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;should a point object be placed from the plano-convex lens, so that position of the final image is independent of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0017_c44c72e505a3.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 111px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
